403
00:27:19,880 --> 00:27:28,980
In 1962, Red Adair, Boots Hanson, and Coots Matthews were facing down a monster of a gas

404
00:27:28,981 --> 00:27:32,380
well fire in Algeria called the Devil's Cigarette Lighter.

405
00:27:33,860 --> 00:27:37,620
That was a tremendous fire, one that went on for several months.

406
00:27:37,700 --> 00:27:42,520
And it was so large and so ferocious that really most people didn't think that it could

407
00:27:42,521 --> 00:27:43,600
ever be controlled.

408
00:27:43,601 --> 00:27:48,100
This roaring giant shot flames and smoke 800 feet

409
00:27:48,200 --> 00:27:52,380
into the air as 550 million cubic feet of gas spewed out

410
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:56,020
each day in the scorching desert heat.

411
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:59,320
The pressure was so great, men had to be careful not to be

412
00:27:59,420 --> 00:28:00,620
sucked up into the flames.

413
00:28:03,760 --> 00:28:04,880
And it was the biggest one.

414
00:28:04,980 --> 00:28:07,700
And she would flare out and try to pick you off the ground,

415
00:28:07,800 --> 00:28:09,300
so much volume coming out.

416
00:28:09,301 --> 00:28:13,600
out. The fire would be a showcase for

417
00:28:13,601 --> 00:28:17,600
the techniques and tools Myron invented and Redd perfected.

418
00:28:17,601 --> 00:28:23,540
Without access to water, the men had to drill for it.

419
00:28:23,541 --> 00:28:29,860
To hold the water, they dug three pits, each about the size

420
00:28:29,861 --> 00:28:33,860
of a football field, and 10 feet deep.

421
00:28:33,861 --> 00:28:37,860
Redd's team cooled the site with high-pressure water cannons

422
00:28:37,861 --> 00:28:43,140
and protected the equipment with corrugated tin.

423
00:28:43,200 --> 00:28:46,760
Red's men used an Athey wagon and bulldozers to pull away the

424
00:28:46,840 --> 00:28:50,180
debris of the burned up rig.

425
00:28:50,240 --> 00:28:53,680
After several months of preparation, they were finally

426
00:28:53,740 --> 00:28:58,320
ready to shoot out the fire with nitroglycerin charges.

427
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:07,860
We shot out 750 pounds of 100% glycerin.

428
00:29:07,861 --> 00:29:11,100
Now that the well was no longer burning,

429
00:29:11,200 --> 00:29:13,760
the men attempted to cap it.

430
00:29:13,860 --> 00:29:17,300
Red employed a sand line cutter,

431
00:29:17,400 --> 00:29:21,800
a tool he had been using for several years.

432
00:29:21,900 --> 00:29:26,220
The sand line cutter was a sand resin-coated cable looped

433
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:27,920
around the well head.

434
00:29:28,020 --> 00:29:30,980
Winches on opposite sides pulled the cable back and forth,

435
00:29:31,080 --> 00:29:33,420
cutting the well head off like a bandsaw.

436
00:29:33,421 --> 00:29:38,420
The men then forced a blowout preventer over the blowing well

437
00:29:38,520 --> 00:29:43,420
and secured it to the pipe, a delicate operation

438
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,960
when even static electricity could reignite the well

439
00:29:47,060 --> 00:29:48,360
and kill everyone around.

440
00:29:54,380 --> 00:29:57,980
Finally, after six months, the Devil's cigarette lighter

441
00:29:58,080 --> 00:29:58,980
stopped roaring.

442
00:30:03,420 --> 00:30:07,420
The amazing feat captured the world's attention and propelled

443
00:30:07,520 --> 00:30:11,660
Red Adair to international celebrity.

444
00:30:11,760 --> 00:30:14,960
Red made television appearances, and Hollywood even produced

445
00:30:15,060 --> 00:30:19,060
the movie Hellfighters, starring John Wayne, which was loosely

446
00:30:19,160 --> 00:30:23,380
based on Red's life. In between Red's celebrity

447
00:30:23,480 --> 00:30:28,520
appearances, he joined Boots and Coots in putting out fires.

448
00:30:28,620 --> 00:30:33,420
These jobs sent them in all directions.

449
00:30:33,421 --> 00:30:36,120
On one occasion, Coutts traveled with Red overseas

450
00:30:36,220 --> 00:30:38,720
to put out a well fire in Africa.

451
00:30:38,820 --> 00:30:42,460
Red, before we could get on the airplane going down

452
00:30:42,560 --> 00:30:44,860
in the desert to down the Algiers,

453
00:30:44,960 --> 00:30:48,060
we got another job in Mexico.

454
00:30:48,160 --> 00:30:51,580
And hell, I turned around and got back on the airplane.

455
00:30:51,680 --> 00:30:53,580
But when he landed in New York,

456
00:30:53,680 --> 00:30:56,480
Coutts learned that the fire in Mexico had gone out

457
00:30:56,580 --> 00:30:58,580
and he wasn't needed anymore.

458
00:30:58,680 --> 00:31:01,220
So I got back on the airplane

459
00:31:01,221 --> 00:31:05,420
and headed back to Paris, and I just got seated on that damn

460
00:31:05,520 --> 00:31:06,220
plane.

461
00:31:06,320 --> 00:31:09,220
This girl asked me, was that my first transatlantic crossing?

462
00:31:09,320 --> 00:31:13,060
I said, well, if I make it, it'd be my third one this day.

463
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,560
And she thought I was a nut.

464
00:31:14,660 --> 00:31:16,560
She never asked me a damn question after that,

465
00:31:16,660 --> 00:31:18,780
but it was the truth.

466
00:31:18,880 --> 00:31:20,780
Despite the camaraderie developed from years

467
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:24,180
of risking their lives together, Boots Hanson

468
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:27,620
and Coots Matthews abruptly departed the Red Adair Company

469
00:31:27,720 --> 00:31:29,880
in 1978.

470
00:31:29,881 --> 00:31:34,080
Their business immediately took off

471
00:31:34,180 --> 00:31:36,620
and became very successful.

472
00:31:36,720 --> 00:31:38,620
He said, what are we going to name the company?

473
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:41,220
I said, we got to call it Boots and Coots.

474
00:31:41,320 --> 00:31:44,720
And he says, how about Coots and Boots?

475
00:31:44,820 --> 00:31:46,700
And I said, of course, the B comes before the C,

476
00:31:46,800 --> 00:31:49,540
so he was the president.

477
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:51,640
Which wasn't a very good honor either.

478
00:31:54,900 --> 00:31:58,040
But they weren't Red's only competition.

479
00:31:58,041 --> 00:32:03,100
In 1975, with 23 years of experience as a drilling engineer,

480
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:08,120
Joe Bowden Sr. started Wild Well Control in Houston.

481
00:32:10,700 --> 00:32:16,460
Bowden's Wild Well Control would grow to become one of the most successful band of blowout specialists in the world.

482
00:32:18,660 --> 00:32:25,880
By the late 1980s, more than half a dozen firefighting companies had formed to meet the demand of the industry worldwide.

483
00:32:25,881 --> 00:32:29,960
With the next generation of firefighters ready to take over,

484
00:32:31,320 --> 00:32:34,760
Red, Boots, and Coots might have been contemplating retirement.

485
00:32:36,200 --> 00:32:38,040
But they'd have to wait just a little longer.

486
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:45,480
In March of 1991, Saddam Hussein created the mother of all oil well fires.

487
00:32:47,320 --> 00:32:51,000
Iraqi soldiers retreating out of occupied Kuwait during the Gulf War

488
00:32:51,560 --> 00:32:53,960
set every oil well they could find on fire.

489
00:32:53,961 --> 00:32:57,960
The country was one gigantic fiery blowout.

490
00:32:58,060 --> 00:33:01,960
The world turned to Texas for help.

491
00:33:02,060 --> 00:33:04,600
We flew all over it looking over it.

492
00:33:04,700 --> 00:33:07,500
When you first get in, it was a heck of a bad looking sight.

493
00:33:09,600 --> 00:33:13,320
Even all of us that have worked on well fires

